Constructor chaining means calling one constructor from another constructor 
so that initialization logic can be reused instead of duplicated.


Constructor Chaining
       │
       ├── this()  → another constructor in the same class // constructor overloading , calling a constructor.
       │
       └── super() → constructor of the parent class // during inheritance 


Ex -
        class Student {

    Student() {
        this("MMB", 17);
        System.out.println("No-arg constructor");
    }

    Student(String name, int age) {
        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
    }
}

In Main -> Student s = new Student();
 Execution Flow of Constructor Chaining
-------------------------------
Student()
   ↓
this("MMB", 17)
   ↓
Student(String, int)
    ↓
    output is : Name: MMB
                Age: 17
                No-arg constructor
